# CLAUDE.local.md (template)

Copy this file to `CLAUDE.local.md` (gitignored) and fill in your local
context. This is where agent-personal memory lives: customer codenames,
infrastructure hostnames, personal preferences, history of work in this
repo. It does NOT get committed.

## Local environment

- Working directory: `<path on disk>`
- Operating system: `<windows|linux|macos>`
- Python: `<command, e.g. py -3.14>`

## Local infrastructure

- Backend host:port: `localhost:8089`
- Snapshot output: `<path or WP uploads dir>`
- Salt file: `~/.multi-agent-snapshot-salt`
- (optional) WordPress install: `<path>`
- (optional) NAS / Docker host: `<hostname>`

## Confidential project codenames

If your AI sessions reference internal projects / clients whose names should
NEVER appear in a public snapshot, list them here. They get scrubbed by
`--public` snapshot mode when listed in your customer-blocklist.

```
<client-1>
<client-2>
<internal-product-codename>
```

## Personal conventions

- Commit-message style: `<your-style>`
- Pre-push checks: `<your-list>`
- Whom to ping when escalating: `<contact>`

## History

Free-form area for your own notes about what was done in this repo. Agents
will read it on session start. Examples of useful entries:

- `2026-NN-NN — refactored estimator to use Codex CLI because Claude headless
  OAuth was broken`
- `2026-NN-NN — decided to keep dashboard single-file vanilla JS (no build)`
- `2026-NN-NN — published v0.1.0 to GitHub`
